--TEST--
`E0303` for a name an `autoload` prefix covers lists every file it looked in, and for a name no prefix covers lists the prefixes — `rule:programs/autoload`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `Shop\Cart` is under the `Shop` prefix, so both of its roots were searched,
// in the order they are written. `Blog\Post` is under no prefix at all.
autoload 'Shop' from './lib', './vendor/shop';
echo Shop\Cart::total(), "\n";
echo Blog\Post::title(), "\n";
--FILE lib/Order.nvs--
<?nvs
namespace Shop;

class Order
{
}
--FILE vendor/shop/Item.nvs--
<?nvs
namespace Shop;

class Item
{
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0303]: `Shop\Cart` is not declared
  --> case.nvs:5:6
  |
5 | echo Shop\Cart::total(), "\n";
  |      ^^^^^^^^^ no matching declaration
  = note: `autoload` looked for `Shop\Cart` in `lib/Cart.nvs`, `vendor/shop/Cart.nvs`

error[E0303]: `Blog\Post` is not declared
  --> case.nvs:6:6
  |
6 | echo Blog\Post::title(), "\n";
  |      ^^^^^^^^^ no matching declaration
  = note: no `autoload` prefix covers `Blog\Post`. The prefixes are `Shop`

error: aborting due to 2 errors
